# jscout never auto-loads this file. Keep non-secret repository policy in
# .jscout.toml; use the process environment only for referenced secrets,
# standard runtime settings, evaluation labels, or temporary legacy migration.
# See docs/installation.md#environment-and-mcp-credentials for launch examples.
# Export a selected key explicitly in the shell that launches jscout/client:
#   export OPENAI_API_KEY='your-key'
# Copying this file to .env is not enough. An already-running GUI MCP client
# may not inherit shell exports; configure its environment and restart it.
# Setup never copies secrets into project MCP configuration.

# Secrets referenced by .jscout.toml. Uncomment only what your selected
# providers use; never commit populated values.
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=
# JSCOUT_EMBED_KEY=
# LOCAL_LLM_API_KEY=

# Standard Node TLS configuration, when a private CA is required.
# NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS=/absolute/path/to/private-ca.pem

# Optional evaluation/telemetry labels. These describe an invocation and are
# intentionally not durable repository policy.
# JSCOUT_SESSION_ID=
# JSCOUT_TASK_ID=
# JSCOUT_PROFILE_LABEL=

# Legacy migration examples. These remain compatibility fallbacks only;
# jscout warns when they supply non-secret settings. Prefer the corresponding
# .jscout.toml fields shown in .jscout.toml.example.
# JSCOUT_LLM_MODEL=openai-codex:gpt-5.6-terra
# JSCOUT_LLM_REASONING=high
# JSCOUT_PI_AI_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://gateway.example.com/v1
# JSCOUT_PI_AI_AUTH_FILE=~/.pi-ai/auth.json
# JSCOUT_EMBED_PROVIDER=local
# JSCOUT_EMBED_MODEL=BAAI/bge-m3
# JSCOUT_INFERENCE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8792
# JSCOUT_RERANK_MODEL=BAAI/bge-reranker-v2-m3
# JSCOUT_TELEMETRY_FILE=.jscout/telemetry.jsonl
